# House lint configuration.
#
# line_length 120 rather than lintr's 80: this package's plot constructors take
# many named arguments and the calls read better whole than wrapped.
#
# object_length 35 rather than lintr's 30: six exported sample-data generators
# are longer than 30 characters, the longest being
# sample_nonparametric_ordinal_points at 35. Renaming an export is a breaking
# change for every package that draws through this one, and the names are
# descriptive rather than careless, so the threshold moves instead.
#
# object_name accepts SNAKE_CASE alongside snake_case: the score-scale
# constants in mirror-histogram.R and .NP_SIM in nonparametric-curve-plot.R
# shout deliberately, so that HVTI_SCORE_MAX is visibly a package constant and
# not a local at every use site.
#
# indentation_linter and commented_code_linter are off. Both fire heavily on
# the aligned-argument style used throughout R/ and on vignette chunks that
# deliberately show an alternative call commented out. Neither catches a defect
# here, and leaving them on buries the linters that do.
#
# Everything else is lintr's default and IS enforced -- commas, infix spaces,
# object usage. The workflow gates on this file, so a lint that is genuinely a
# false positive belongs behind a `# nolint` carrying the reason, not behind a
# widened rule here.
linters: linters_with_defaults(
    line_length_linter = line_length_linter(120L),
    object_length_linter = object_length_linter(35L),
    object_name_linter = object_name_linter(c("snake_case", "SNAKE_CASE", "symbols")),
    indentation_linter = NULL,
    commented_code_linter = NULL
  )
